N2  - Introduction: The menopausal transition is characterized by physical and psychological symptoms which affect negatively women’s well-being and health-related quality of life (HRQoL). Life-style patterns as nutritional status and dietary habits are highly associated with several quality-of-life parameters during menopause. Objectives: To investigate possible associations between dietary patterns and HRQoL among healthy menopausal women. Methods: 384 healthy postmenopausal women without clinically overt chronic disease recruited consecutively from the Menopause Clinic of Aretaieio Hospital of Athens were evaluated in a cross-sectional design. Demographic characteristics and anthropometric parameters were recorded. Dietary intake was assessed by a validated food frequency questionnaire. Adherence to the Mediterranean diet was evaluated through a relevant score. Self-reported HRQoL was assessed by using the 12-Item Short-Form Health Survey (SF-12). Results: The physical HRQoL was negatively related to the body mass index (r=-0.176, p=0.001), the participant’s age (r=-0.202; p=0.000) and the years since menopause (r=-0.227;p=0.000). The frequency of coffee/tea consumption was positively associated with the physical HRQoL (r=0.182, p=0.001). After further adjustment for potential confounders, multivariable linear regression showed that the frequency of fruit consumption was negatively associated with the physical HRQoL (b-coefficient=-0,138; p=0,031). The positive association between the coffee/tea consumption and the physical HRQoL remained statistically significant after the model adjustment (b-coefficient=0.135; p=0.021). No statistical significance was found between HRQoL parameters and Mediterranean dietary pattern, as well as the frequency of meal consumption or dietary supplement intake. Conclusions: Parameters of daily dietary intake are associated with physical HRQoL among post-menopausal women. The significance of these findings should be evaluated in further studies. Keywords: menopause, diet, health-related quality of life, dietary pattern.
