N2  - The proceedings contain 40 papers. The topics discussed include: QATO-CHAD - a brief instrument to measure addiction to overeating in children and adolescents; eating styles and adiposity in 4-6 year-olds: do maternal feeding practices and health cognitions matter?; how to promote fruit and vegetable consumption in schools: a toolkit; splendid: preventing obesity and eating disorders through behavioural monitoring and normalization; dietary habits of overweight and obese children and adherence to the Mediterranean diet; food choices from school canteens. data from the hellenic action plan for the assessment, prevention and treatment for childhood obesity (MIS 301205); nutri-face; a pilot intervention study on adolescent dietary habits and physical activity levels through Facebook; the impact of body mass index at menarcheal age. data from the hellenic action plan for the assessment, prevention and treatment for childhood obesity (MIS 301205); the prevalence of hypertension in school-age children and adolescents with intellectual disabilities in southeastern Poland; screening for MC4R mutations in Cypriot children with severe early onset obesity and tall stature identified a novel MC4R deletion; family history of cardiovascular disease and waist circumference in a sample of overweight/obese Greek children and adolescents; combining biomedical, nutritional and physical fitness parameters in a school-based intervention study - preliminary data from the Moyo-study Salzburg; and preliminary results from a dietary intervention in obese prepubertal children.
