N2  - As a part of aging so called inflammatory processes play a fundamental role, in a negative way. Polyphenols; like isoflavones, resveratrol, lycopene and hydroxytyrosol; are anti-inflammatory plant compounds and they can be found in spices, herbs, fruits and vegetables. In addition to those, oils rich in omega-3-fatty acids are also very important for a healthy diet in the menopause. The reduction of carbohydrates with an high glycemic index is essential. To be specific; sugar, starch and oils rich in omega-6-fatty acids should be avoided, because of their high inflammatory effect. For this reason, we will discuss why the traditional mediterranean and asian cuisines are the ideal anti-inflammatory diets and why we need to emphasize the importance of nutrition during menopause. Chronic silent inflammation leads to age-related diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, cancer, Alzheimer's and insulin resistance. The words of the most famous doctor of ancient Rome - Aulus Cornelius Celsus, have not lost its validity: “Let food be your medicine”.
